# Slice 296 probe (ABSENT-HEAD-WRITE-NORM): at the unit's root a head nothing binds, with a name as its tail (`x: j`), is a
# named Structure with the written content `j`; `call: x` executes it (no effect), the program goes on.  Entry 7.
int: j 3
x: j
int: code 7
call: x
if: j != 3
    code: 1
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
